<p>All monetary attributes were declared using the decimal(18,2) column type
rather than a floating-point type, in order to avoid the rounding errors th=
at
binary floating-point representations can introduce into financial
calculations. Foreign key relationships, for example between Payment and Sa=
le,
or between Property and Project, were declared using Entity Framework Core's
fluent configuration in ApplicationDbContext, ensuring that the database it=
self
rejects orphaned records, in line with the referential integrity principle
discussed in Section 2.1.</p>

<h2><span style=3D'mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>4.6 Implement=
ation
of modules<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

<p>The system is organised into twelve functional modules, each represented=
 by
a dedicated MVC controller and, where the module involves non-trivial busin=
ess
rules, a corresponding service class. Table 4.6 lists the five user roles
implemented through ASP.NET Core Identity and the modules each role is
authorised to access.</p>

